1
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Power. Grace. Wisdom. Wonder.

2
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Wonder Woman is a action, adventure, fantasy film directed by Patty Jenkins.

3
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:12,000
An Amazon princess comes to the world of Man in the grips of the First World War
to confront the forces of evil and bring an end to human conflict.

4
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Diana Prince / Wonder Woman, played by Gal Gadot.

5
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:36,000
Steve Trevor, played by Chris Pine.

6
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:18,000
Hippolyta, played by Connie Nielsen.

7
00:32:54,000 --> 00:33:00,000
Antiope, played by Robin Wright.

8
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:42,000
Ludendorff, played by Danny Huston.

9
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:24,000
Sir Patrick / Ares, played by David Thewlis.

10
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Wonder Woman is a 2017 superhero film based on the character from DC Comics.

11
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:48,000
Directed by Patty Jenkins from a screenplay by Allan Heinberg, based on a story by Heinberg, Zack
Snyder, and Jason Fuchs, it is the fourth installment in the DC Extended Universe (DCEU).

12
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
Gal Gadot stars as the title character, alongside Chris Pine, Robin Wright,
Danny Huston, David Thewlis, Connie Nielsen, and Elena Anaya.

13
01:01:06,000 --> 01:01:12,000
Depicting the character's origin story, the film follows Diana, an Amazon princess, who leaves her home island of Themyscira during
World War I after American pilot and spy Steve Trevor crash-lands on the island and informs her about the ongoing conflict.

14
01:05:48,000 --> 01:05:54,000
Believing the war is orchestrated by Ares, the god of war, she
sets out to stop him and end the suffering.

15
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:36,000
Development of a live-action Wonder Woman film began in 1996, with Ivan
Reitman initially set to produce and possibly direct.

16
01:15:12,000 --> 01:15:18,000
The project remained in development hell for many years, with writers and directors
like Jon Cohen, Todd Alcott, and Joss Whedon attached at various points.

17
01:19:54,000 --> 01:20:00,000
Warner Bros.

18
01:24:36,000 --> 01:24:42,000
officially announced the film in 2010, and Patty
Jenkins was hired as director in 2015.

19
01:29:18,000 --> 01:29:24,000
The film drew inspiration from William Moulton Marston's 1940s Wonder Woman stories,
George Pérez's 1980s comics, and the New 52 version of the character.

20
01:34:00,000 --> 01:34:06,000
Principal photography began on November 21, 2015, in the United
Kingdom, France, and Italy, concluding on May 9, 2016.

21
01:38:42,000 --> 01:38:48,000
Additional filming occurred in November 2016.

22
01:43:24,000 --> 01:43:30,000
Wonder Woman premiered at the Pantages Theatre in Hollywood on May 26,
2017, and was released in the United States by Warner Bros.

23
01:48:06,000 --> 01:48:12,000
Pictures on June 2.

24
01:52:48,000 --> 01:52:54,000
The film received critical acclaim for its direction, performances, visuals, story, action
sequences, and cultural significance, though some criticism was directed at the climax.

25
01:57:30,000 --> 01:57:36,000
It grossed over $824 million worldwide, making it the tenth highest-grossing film of 2017 and the
highest-grossing film by a solo female director until it was surpassed by Barbie (2023).

26
02:02:12,000 --> 02:02:18,000
The American Film Institute included it in its top ten films of 2017, and it
won the Hugo Award for Best Dramatic Presentation in 2018.

27
02:06:54,000 --> 02:07:00,000
A sequel, Wonder Woman 1984, was released in December 2020, with Patty Jenkins returning as director
and Gal Gadot, Chris Pine, Robin Wright, and Connie Nielsen reprising their roles.

28
02:11:36,000 --> 02:11:42,000
Plans for a third film were canceled after DC Films was
restructured into DC Studios in 2022.

29
02:16:18,000 --> 02:16:24,000
The film explores themes of island, hero, strong
woman, world war i, empowerment.
